Jev Shadow notices
==================

This project is an independent, experimental spike. It is not affiliated with
or endorsed by any of the vendors named below. It contains no vendor SDKs,
service code, or credentials.

Hermes (Nous Research)
----------------------

This harness is designed to run in-process inside Hermes and, in that mode,
calls Hermes' own egress redactor rather than shipping a competing
secret-pattern list. That dependency is on a *host-provided callable*, not on
Hermes source code: the harness accepts any `Callable[[str], str]` via the
`redactor` argument and never vendors or imports Hermes files itself. See
`src/jev_shadow/redaction.py::resolve_redactor` for the injection contract and
`vendor/VENDOR.md` in the Hermes plugin integration for the vendored copy.

TypeSafe / Jev
--------------

Jev and TypeSafe are product names of their respective owners. This project
calls the TypeSafe "System One" endpoint only when a caller explicitly opts in
with a credential, and does not include their SDKs, service code, or
credentials. No API key is ever committed, logged, or written to disk by this
package.

Note on this repository's own telemetry metric names
----------------------------------------------------

The metrics exported here (`jev_shadow_*`) share a namespace with the separate
`ianlintner/jev-router` project, whose exporter already uses some of the same
metric names with different label schemas. Both are intended to be scraped by
one Prometheus. See the "Telemetry namespace collision" section of README.md
before enabling both exporters on the same Prometheus instance.
